# Tests

When behavior changes, add or update tests in the same change.

From repo root:
- Unit: `pnpm test`
- Types: `pnpm typecheck`
- Lint: `pnpm lint`
- E2E: `pnpm test:e2e`
- Rust: `pnpm rust:check` for orchestrator/infra Rust.

Follow sibling test style (Vitest/Playwright/etc. already in that package). Do not add a second test runner.
`packages/ide` uses its own tooling — do not assume root `pnpm test` covers it.

## Run the full suites once, at the end

Iterate on the single test file covering your change; run `pnpm typecheck` and a
full `pnpm test` when the change is otherwise finished. `apps/web` is cheap
(~20s typecheck, ~45s tests). `packages/ide` is minutes — be sparing there, and
scope it: `vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/<area>`.

## Test environment

`apps/web/vitest.config.ts` runs two projects: `lib` on `node` with no setup
file, `components` on `jsdom` with Testing Library. Pure-logic tests go under
`lib/`. Do not restore a global `jsdom` environment — booting a DOM for tests
that never touch one cost this suite 4x its runtime (253s to 45s).

`apps/web/lib/retired/` is excluded from both the typecheck and the vitest `lib`
project. Code there is unverified and must not be imported.
